"""Storage for the cezanne: what fills the phone, as Android's storage page
shows it. One bar for the used space and a list of categories:
  Apps        installed apps (packages with an app in the app grid; their
              size from pacman's database), their data in the hidden folders
              of the home directory (~/.config/<app>, ~/.local/share/<app>,
              ~/.<app>), /opt and Flatpak
  Games       Steam's library (steamapps/common, the Proton prefixes)
  Images, Videos, Audio, Documents & other
              the files of the home directory outside hidden folders, by
              their extension
  Cache       ~/.cache, cache folders inside app data, Steam's shader and
              download caches, /var/cache, /var/tmp
  Trash       the trash
  System      everything else: the system's packages, /etc, /var, /boot
Each category opens a page: folders and the largest files, apps with their
data and cache (cache can be cleared), games, cache folders (clearable),
the trash (emptied), the system's largest packages.

The whole root file system is walked by worker processes of this script
(--scan-worker; Python threads would serialise on the interpreter lock):
the tree is cut into units at known large folders and handed out to the
first worker that is free, each sends back its totals. Sizes are the
allocated sizes of the files before btrfs compression (what du reports), so
they add up to more than the used space the bar shows. Folders this user
cannot read (other users, /root) are left out.

What the files take on disk needs root: only root may search btrfs' trees
for a file's extent items (compressed size, type), as compsize does. When
polkit lets the active session run the installed script as root
(org.cezanne.storage.policy: pkexec ... --root-worker, no password), the
workers run that way and also total the extents per category and folder
(one tree search per file, against its folder's descriptor), and every
page shows the size on disk and its share. The root workers take the home
folder from pkexec's caller, never from the arguments, and only send back
totals and the caller's own largest files.
"""
